msgstr ""

msgid "A program to input a value"
msgstr ""

msgid "If we would like to write a program that takes a number from the user, we would use `cin` as follows."
msgstr ""

msgid "In line 5, we declare an integer variable named `value` as we would do in C."
msgstr ""

msgid "In line 8, `cin` is standard input stream used to get user input, and `>>` is the operator used to get the user input and store it in the variable to the right of `>>`, which is `value`."
msgstr ""

msgid "In line 10, we use `cout` to output the string `\"The value entered is \"` followed by `value`. To follow the string by the value stored in a variable, you have to put a `<<` before the variable."
